               <occupation type="literary">He was a scholar focusing primarily on customary law, traditional land right and land resources,
                  genealogies, and pastoral taxonomy. He was in assiduous correspondence with <persName ref="PRS3182ContiRo"/>, who 
                  published several articles based on his research.</occupation>
               <birth when="1910-07-17">17 July 1910</birth>
               <death when="1942">In June 1942, he was made war prisoner by the British troops and sent to South Africa. He died as the ship
                  that transported him was sunk by the German navy.</death>
               <floruit notBefore="1936" notAfter="1942">He was colonial officer of the Italian East Africa serving in several posts in 
